WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.701
-Welcome, welcome, welcome,
welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:05.501
Thank you for being here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:08.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:10.801
Well, guys, this is exciting.
Sunday is Mother's Day.

00:00:10.801 --> 00:00:13.400
And we love
all the moms out there.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:16.701
Yeah, I read that, this year,

00:00:16.701 --> 00:00:20.400
the average person is spending
$245 on Mother's Day.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:21.601
-Ooh!

00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:22.801
&gt;&gt; Yeah, and on Father's Day,

00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:24.601
that same person will be like,
"I don't know.

00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:29.100
Should we get him two
$5 scratch-offs or one $10..."

00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:32.801
Of course, the best Mother's Day
gift costs nothing at all,

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:36.033
but if you're 40 and still
handing out "free hug" coupons,

00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:37.300
might be time to up your game.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.567
You know what I'm saying?

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:40.100
"I'll do some chores for free."

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.367
She's like, "Please move out."

00:00:44.667 --> 00:00:47.067
As always, Hooters
is celebrating Mother's Day

00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:50.300
by offering moms
10 free boneless wings.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.901
-Aww!

00:00:51.901 --> 00:00:53.501
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:57.267
And this is nice.

00:00:57.267 --> 00:00:58.601
If you take your mom to Hooters,

00:00:58.601 --> 00:01:00.901
she'll be seated in
a special crying section

00:01:00.901 --> 00:01:04.634
for moms whose kids brought
them to Hooters on Mother's Day.

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:06.701
Well, I read that 20%
of moms say that

00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:09.968
they've been disappointed before
by their Mother's Day gifts,

00:01:09.968 --> 00:01:13.968
while the other 80% were just
passive-aggressive about it.

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:16.434
"I'm sure this was
the best she could do."

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.534
Some more fun news
for the weekend.

00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:22.434
Tomorrow is
the 148th Kentucky Derby.

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:23.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:26.300
Finally!

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:30.400
Finally a day for Americans
to drink and gamble.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:31.767
You know what I'm saying?
Finally.

00:01:31.767 --> 00:01:32.901
Well, get this.

00:01:32.901 --> 00:01:34.868
I heard that NBC
is going to have four hours

00:01:34.868 --> 00:01:37.133
of coverage before the race.

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:40.367
Four hours leading up to
two exciting minutes,

00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:42.334
or, as that's also known,
my wedding night.

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:43.868
Hey!
-Hey! Oh!

00:01:43.868 --> 00:01:46.868
-What? Hey, who wrote that?
-Hey!

00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:49.267
-Oh, my wife? Oh.
-Oh, man.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.000
I saw that
former president Trump

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.133
will be at the Kentucky Derby.

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:57.200
So don't be surprised
when the race is over

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:01.267
and it takes two months
to decide the winner.

00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:02.467
[ As Trump ]
It was totally rigged.

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:05.534
It was Sugar Cube
that should have won.

00:02:05.534 --> 00:02:07.234
That's right -- Trump is
going to be at the Derby,

00:02:07.234 --> 00:02:09.334
and while he's there,
he's hosting a fundraiser

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:12.567
that costs $75,000 to attend.

00:02:12.567 --> 00:02:14.968
Yep, for 75 grand,
you get to meet Trump,

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:17.868
and it's all the
horse dewormer you can eat.

00:02:19.901 --> 00:02:21.801
Well, guys, some big movie news.

00:02:21.801 --> 00:02:26.300
The new "Doctor Strange"
sequel has finally hit theaters.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:27.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:27.901 --> 00:02:30.000
All I'm saying is,
if you take your mom to Hooters

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.367
and then "Doctor Strange,"
you better nail her birthday.

00:02:32.367 --> 00:02:33.367
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:33.367 --> 00:02:35.300
I'm just warning you guys.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.601
The full title of the movie is

00:02:36.601 --> 00:02:40.000
"Doctor Strange in
the Multiverse of Madness."

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.534
It's pretty long,
although it got worse when

00:02:41.534 --> 00:02:42.634
they tried to shorten it
on the marquee.

00:02:42.634 --> 00:02:44.868
"Dr. Strange in the --" Oh, wow.

00:02:44.868 --> 00:02:46.467
-Oh!

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:48.901
That would be
a good Mother's Day present.

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:51.100
-No, I...

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:52.167
Hey, this is cool.

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:54.367
I saw that today
is National Nurses Day.

00:02:54.367 --> 00:02:55.934
-Yeah! Hey!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:57.868 --> 00:02:59.801
Come on!

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:06.267
-And as per usual, there's a
doctor stealing their thunder.

00:03:07.667 --> 00:03:09.400
Hey, did you guys
hear about this?

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:13.100
Police in Switzerland seized
over half a ton of cocaine

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:17.200
that was found hidden in coffee
beans at an espresso plant.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:20.400
Yeah. Then every
coffee snob was like, "Ugh!

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.934
Real Italians
grind their own cocaine."

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:26.734
And, finally,
on a road in Missouri,

00:03:26.734 --> 00:03:31.267
a truck overturned and spilled
44,000 pounds of hard seltzer.

00:03:31.267 --> 00:03:34.367
44,000 pounds of hard seltzer
spilled on the road.

00:03:34.367 --> 00:03:36.801
It's the first case of people
driving over the influence.

